  "reasoning": "Recent searches did not return any usable 2026-cycle head\u2011to\u2011head polling or forecaster ratings for specific West Virginia federal races, so the best available evidence is the state\u2019s recent presidential results and structural partisan index.[1][11][15] In 2020, Donald Trump carried West Virginia by roughly 68.6% to 26.5%, a margin of about 42.1 points, and the statewide Cook Partisan Voting Index is around R+21, marking it as one of the most Republican states in the country.[1][11][15] Given this very large and persistent Republican advantage and the absence of any recent evidence of competitive federal races, West Virginia currently leans strongly Republican for federal elections.",
